+        /* NOTE (2026-08-20 night-verify): a `verticalRange *= factor` 3DS overscan was
+           tried here to close the distant-sky black wedge (docs/research/
+           sky-backdrop-wedge-analysis.md) and PROVEN INEFFECTIVE on the emulator: the
+           GDX_DIAG_SKY [sky] topGap held ~0.31 identically at factors 1.41x AND 2.70x.
+           Root cause: Background_UpdateSkyboxVtx clamps every skybox vertex position to
+           +/-32000.0f (s16 vertex-coord range). At F-Zero X's skyboxDepth the verts
+           already saturate that clamp, so scaling verticalRange only pushes them further
+           past a fixed ceiling -- the on-screen quad does not grow. The real fix must
+           reduce skyboxDepth (and rescale coverage to stay inside +/-32000) or rework the
+           projection, which re-frames the whole backdrop and overlaps the geometry/roof
+           domain; deferred. The visible top/bottom black band in scanouts is largely the
+           fixed scanout letterbox (present on menu/title too), not skybox undercoverage. */
+
         xScale = camera->xzNormalizedX;
         zScale = camera->xzNormalizedZ;
         xOffset = background->scrollDepth * xScale;
